      "writtenOn": "2021-10-15T11:41:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess one part I\u0027m not sure about is that the userspace process could now modify the data buffer while we are parsing objects. For example, it could perhaps change offsets in one of the _PTR types right after we have verified that it is correct and doesn\u0027t refer to an earlier object. Do you think this is an issue? I need to give it a bit more thought.",
      "revId": "259e50486df11eb1377b28864928b2d508981e0f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c162be6d_fc4076ff",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-15T21:33:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. Good one. I think it isn\u0027t an issue for the cases where we read the user ptr once, verify it and write the fixed-up version. We just wouldn\u0027t see the modification since we never look at it again. But we do have at least 1 case where we go back and re-read the source proc version of the PTR in preparation for calling binder_translate_fd_array() (the 2nd patch in this series).\n\nIn this case, the source proc could corrupt uparent-\u003ebuffer which would result in a bogus address for copy_from_user() when we read each untranslated fd from the array. This corruption would either result in bogus fds if the pointer is valid or EFAULT if it isn\u0027t.\n\nEFAULT would fail gracefully. Bogus fds might accidentally work (in which case the target has some random fds open which no doubt would cause issues). If any fd is invalid, the transaction would fail when the fd fixups are applied.\n\nSince the source process could pass bogus fds any time it wants anyway, this failure mode seems reasonable for a source process that misbehaves in this way.\n\nDo you see any other ways this could bite us?",
      "parentUuid": "e396d67e_77cc843a",
      "revId": "259e50486df11eb1377b28864928b2d508981e0f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62ecba0b_985cc4bf",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
